It also covers permanent residence. Carl Wurfel is director, and its consultants have worked in the field for over ten years. The firm handles study permits and spousal sponsorship and acts for individuals, families and employers. It serves Edmonton, Sherwood Park, St. Albert, Spruce Grove, Stony Plain, Leduc and surrounding Alberta communities, and many clients come through referrals from friends and family.','dynamic','live',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO firms (slug,name,city,province,region,featured,rating,review_count,lat,lng,data,hours,about,page_mode,status,created_by) VALUES ('olalere-law-office-ottawa','Olalere Law Office','Ottawa','ON','eastern',0,4.9,319,45.4099895,-75.6983358,'{"name":"Olalere Law Office","city":"Ottawa","featured":false,"tags":["Immigration"],"caseTypes":["immigration"],"region":"eastern","province":"ON","lat":45.4099895,"lng":-75.6983358,"address":"508 Gladstone Ave Ste 206, Ottawa, ON K1R 5P1","phone":"+16139618406","rating":4.9,"count":319,"slug":"olalere-law-office-ottawa","mapsUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Olalere+Law+Office+Ottawa+Ontario","dirUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=508+Gladstone+Ave+Ste+206%2C+Ottawa%2C+ON+K1R+5P1","website":"https://www.ottawaimmigrationlawyers.com","blurb":"Immigration in Ottawa. Rated 4.9 from 319 Google reviews.","type":"logo","src":"images/logos/olalere-law-office-ottawa.png","details":{"founded":2004,"languages":["English"],"lawyers":[{"name":"Kehinde Olalere"},{"name":"Taiwo Olalere"}],"areas":["Immigration law","Immigration appeals","Judicial review"],"serving":["Ottawa"]}}','{"1":[["10:00","18:00"]],"2":[["10:00","18:00"]],"3":[["10:00","18:00"]],"4":[["10:00","18:00"]],"5":[["10:00","18:00"]]}','Olalere Law Office is an Ottawa immigration firm concentrating on appeals of refused applications and removal orders.

Appeals go before the Immigration and Refugee Board and the Federal Court. The practice dates to 2004 and is led by twin brothers Kehinde and Taiwo Olalere, who both studied law and political science at Carleton University. Appeal routes include the Immigration Appeal Division for refused sponsorships and the Refugee Appeal Division for negative refugee decisions. As a full-service firm it also handles family sponsorship, Express Entry, study and work permits, visitor visas, citizenship, humanitarian and compassionate applications and inadmissibility, and publishes selected decisions.','dynamic','live',NULL);
