HIMPRO is the personal injury division of Himelfarb Proszanski, whose wider practice includes business, corporate commercial, real estate and litigation work. HIMPRO lawyers focus on personal injury, disability and insurance law and act for clients in Toronto, Brampton, Hamilton, Kitchener, Oshawa and surrounding areas. The firm has helped individuals, families and businesses for over 30 years, and its fees depend on the outcome of the case.','dynamic','live',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO firms (slug,name,city,province,region,featured,rating,review_count,lat,lng,data,hours,about,page_mode,status,created_by) VALUES ('lamont-law-hamilton','Lamont Law','Hamilton','ON','hamilton-niagara',0,4.8,93,43.2504928,-79.8740293,'{"name":"Lamont Law","city":"Hamilton","featured":false,"tags":["Personal Injury"],"caseTypes":["injury"],"region":"hamilton-niagara","province":"ON","lat":43.2504928,"lng":-79.8740293,"address":"44 Charlton Ave W, Hamilton, ON L8P 2C1","phone":"+19055296668","rating":4.8,"count":93,"slug":"lamont-law-hamilton","mapsUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Lamont+Law+Hamilton+Ontario","dirUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=44+Charlton+Ave+W%2C+Hamilton%2C+ON+L8P+2C1","website":"https://lamontlaw.ca","blurb":"Personal Injury in Hamilton. Rated 4.8 from 93 Google reviews.","type":"logo","src":"images/logos/lamont-law-hamilton.png","details":{"lawyers":[{"name":"Erica Lamont","title":"Lawyer"},{"name":"Braden Adsett","title":"Lawyer"}],"areas":["Brain injuries","Car accidents","Spinal cord injuries","Pedestrian accidents","Bicycle accidents","Slip and falls","Dog attacks","Wrongful death","Long-term disability denials","Medical negligence"],"serving":["Hamilton"]}}',NULL,'Lamont Law is a Hamilton personal injury firm that focuses on serious and catastrophic injuries, accident benefits and long-term disability denials.

Cases for Hamilton and the GTA include motor vehicle accidents, dog attacks, slip and falls, medical and nursing home negligence, wrongful death, brain injuries and spinal cord injuries, and the firm only takes catastrophic injury matters with an estimated value above $50,000. Erica Lamont, who was born in Hamilton, studied at the University of Waterloo and the University of Calgary and was admitted to the Law Society of Ontario in 2014. She is joined by lawyer Braden Adsett and paralegals Carrie Stewart and Phil Vivian.','dynamic','live',NULL);
