Its lawyers have more than three decades of combined experience serving clients in Canada and abroad, and the firm acts for people in Calgary and surrounding areas. The team includes Jide Kupoluyi and Ola Ogbonna. Real estate work covers residential and commercial purchases and sales, while the business practice is aimed at owners and entrepreneurs, whom the lawyers understand because they run businesses themselves. Immigration work covers temporary visas, permanent residence and citizenship, and the office also offers notary public and commissioner for oaths services.','dynamic','live',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO firms (slug,name,city,province,region,featured,rating,review_count,lat,lng,data,hours,about,page_mode,status,created_by) VALUES ('kirk-law-office-ottawa','Kirk Law Office','Ottawa','ON','eastern',0,4.9,81,45.4121285,-75.6812148,'{"name":"Kirk Law Office","city":"Ottawa","featured":false,"tags":["Real Estate"],"caseTypes":["realestate"],"region":"eastern","province":"ON","lat":45.4121285,"lng":-75.6812148,"address":"34 Hawthorne Ave, Ottawa, ON K1S 0B1","phone":"+16132388006","rating":4.9,"count":81,"slug":"kirk-law-office-ottawa","mapsUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Kirk+Law+Office+Ottawa+Ontario","dirUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=34+Hawthorne+Ave%2C+Ottawa%2C+ON+K1S+0B1","website":"https://www.kirklawoffice.ca","blurb":"Real Estate in Ottawa. Rated 4.9 from 81 Google reviews.","type":"logo","src":"images/logos/kirk-law-office-ottawa.png","details":{"languages":["English","French","Ukrainian","Polish","Russian"],"lawyers":[{"name":"Leslie J. Kirk"},{"name":"Iuliia Shulakewych"}],"areas":["Residential real estate","Wills","Powers of attorney","Estate administration","Estate planning"]}}',NULL,'Kirk Law Office is an Ottawa practice handling residential real estate, wills, powers of attorney and estate administration.

Team members are fluent in English, French, Ukrainian, Polish and Russian. On the real estate side the office acts for private lenders and for buyers and sellers of new and resale properties, including condominiums, recreational properties, vacant or development land and investment properties, and it drafts leases and agreements of purchase and sale. Leslie J. Kirk, an Ottawa native, was admitted to the Ontario bar in 2009 after articling with the City of Ottawa''s legal department; her work includes rent-to-own transactions, multi-unit residential sales and RRSP-funded mortgages. Iuliia Shulakewych, who holds the TEP designation, is also on the team.','dynamic','live',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO firms (slug,name,city,province,region,featured,rating,review_count,lat,lng,data,hours,about,page_mode,status,created_by) VALUES ('apna-law-llp-burnaby','Apna Law LLP','Burnaby','BC','bc-burnaby',0,4.7,84,49.2013947,-122.9849304,'{"name":"Apna Law LLP","city":"Burnaby","featured":false,"tags":["Family Law","Civil Litigation"],"caseTypes":["family","litigation"],"region":"bc-burnaby","province":"BC","lat":49.2013947,"lng":-122.9849304,"address":"5489 Byrne Rd Ste 272, Burnaby, BC V5J 3J1","phone":"+16043984168","rating":4.7,"count":84,"slug":"apna-law-llp-burnaby","mapsUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Apna+Law+LLP+Burnaby+British+Columbia","dirUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=5489+Byrne+Rd+Ste+272%2C+Burnaby%2C+BC+V5J+3J1","website":"https://apnalaw.ca","blurb":"Family Law / Civil Litigation in Burnaby. Rated 4.7 from 84 Google reviews.","type":"logo","src":"images/logos/apna-law-llp-burnaby.png","bioImage":"images/bio/apna-law-llp-burnaby.webp","details":{"founded":2018,"areas":["Family law","Estate litigation","Civil litigation","Personal injury law","Mediation and dispute resolution"]}}',NULL,'Apna Law LLP is a Burnaby firm of trial and appellate lawyers handling family, estate, personal injury and civil disputes.

The firm opened in 2018 and serves British Columbia and Alberta, and its lawyers have more than 40 years of combined experience inside and outside the courtroom. Its name is a Punjabi word loosely meaning ours, which the firm links to community and collaboration. The family law team includes James Gill, Amanda James, Hannah Gowans and Ingrid Lee, and an appeal to the Court of Appeal is not a re-hearing of the case. It also publishes articles, including one on international students and immigration consultants.','dynamic','live',NULL);
