Me Yves Paré has more than 30 years of practice in corporate, commercial and transactional law, mainly for small and medium-sized businesses in manufacturing and services and for professionals such as dentists, audiologists and physicians. He has represented pharmacist-owners from across Quebec for over 15 years and knows the pharmacy sector. Other work includes family trusts, asset protection trusts, mergers, dissolutions, due diligence and financing, with Me Alexandre Duquette also on the team.','dynamic','live',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO firms (slug,name,city,province,region,featured,rating,review_count,lat,lng,data,hours,about,page_mode,status,created_by) VALUES ('me-chiraz-ouni-montreal','Me Chiraz Ouni','Montreal','QC','qc-montreal',0,4.8,15,45.5338613,-73.659871,'{"name":"Me Chiraz Ouni","city":"Montreal","featured":false,"tags":["Family Law","Immigration"],"caseTypes":["family","immigration"],"region":"qc-montreal","province":"QC","lat":45.5338613,"lng":-73.659871,"address":"9440 D Bd de l''Acadie, Montréal, QC H4N 1L7","phone":"+15147269881","rating":4.8,"count":15,"slug":"me-chiraz-ouni-montreal","mapsUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Me+Chiraz+Ouni+Montreal+Quebec","dirUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=9440+D+Bd+de+l%27Acadie%2C+Montr%C3%A9al%2C+QC+H4N+1L7","website":"https://www.chirazouni-avocat.ca","blurb":"Family Law / Immigration in Montreal. Rated 4.8 from 15 Google reviews.","type":"logo","src":"images/logos/me-chiraz-ouni-montreal.png","details":{"lawyers":[{"name":"Chiraz Ouni"}],"areas":["Immigration","Droit de la famille","Droit civil","Résidence permanente","Parrainage","Divorce","Garde d''enfant","Pension alimentaire","Patrimoine familial","Petites créances"],"serving":["Montréal"]}}',NULL,'Immigration, family law and civil law are the work of Me Chiraz Ouni, a Montreal lawyer serving students, workers, families and refugees.

Her immigration work includes the Quebec Acceptance Certificate (CAQ), study permits, open and closed work permits, the Quebec skilled worker and Quebec Experience programs, sponsorship, permanent residence and citizenship certificates. In family law she acts in contested and amicable divorces and for de facto spouses, with access rights, custody changes, grandparents'' rights and child and spousal support. Civil matters include lease termination and unpaid rent. She has more than ten years of experience and is a member of the Barreau du Québec.','dynamic','live',NULL);
